[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 475,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 432,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67445,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 432,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cardiac lipoma is a benign mesenchymal tumour of mature adipocytes. Lipomatous hypertrophy of the atrial septum (LHAS) is a collection of immature (brown) fat, mature (yellow) fat, and atrial myocytes, expanding the atrial septum.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 476,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 433,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67446,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 433,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8850/0 Lipoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 477,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 434,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67447,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 434,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F01 &amp; XH1PL8 Benign neoplasm of intrathoracic organs &amp; Lipoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 478,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 435,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67448,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 435,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> fibrolipoma; sclerosed lipoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 479,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 436,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67449,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 436,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67450,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lipomas are most often epicardial but may be endocardial, intracavitary, or pericardial. They can be also intramyocardial, although less commonly {26817909; 26576979; 16047131}. LHAS is a collection of fatty tissue located within the atrial septum.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67451,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The majority of cardiac lipomas are solitary asymptomatic masses discovered incidentally on imaging or autopsy, but rare cases may be associated with arrhythmias, chest pain, syncope, or sudden death {24996689; 19211255; 18350920; 29992619}. There is variable echogenicity by echocardiogram, and MRI/CT should facilitate diagnosis {22025640; 18350920; 2030616; 21642661; 27277840}.</p>\r\n<p>LHAS is generally asymptomatic and discovered incidentally. Occasionally, atrial arrhythmias have been attributed to lipomatous hypertrophy {16519573}. Rarely, the hypertrophy can become large enough to cause obstruction of blood flow within the heart.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67452,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lipomas of the heart are rare, representing 0.5&ndash;3% of excised cardiac tumours, although surgical prevalence is probably an underestimation because cardiac lipomas do not usually require resection {18824772; 14672772; 17670419; 11316130; 14507576; 17218211; 8219826}. All ages are affected, and there is no sex predilection.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67453,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Little is known about the etiology of cardiac lipomas. It is hypothesized that, similar to in extracardiac lipomas, reactivated expression of the high-mobility group AT-hook&nbsp;2 (HMGA2) protein plays a role. This hypothesis is supported by the finding of <em>HMGA2</em> rearrangement in a cardiac lipoma {10747931; 15593017; 24996689} and in a case of LHAS, raising the possibility that a subset of LHAS cases may represent a clonal adipocytic process, or (less probably) lipomas may rarely arise within LHAS {24996689}. A large epicardial lipoma with a novel t(2;19)(p13;p13.2) has also been reported, and there is a single case report of a right atrial lipoma arising in a patient with Cowden syndrome {10824997; 20852328}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67454,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67455,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lipomas are encapsulated, yellow, smooth, soft masses with a yellow glistening cut surface. LHAS is a somewhat related entity involving the atrial septum, with a similar gross appearance otherwise. It often imparts a dumbbell appearance to the septum.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67456,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Histological examination of cardiac lipoma reveals a proliferation of mature adipocytes with a fibrous capsule and variable septa. Rare entrapped myocytes may be seen at the periphery of the lesion. LHAS is characterized by an unencapsulated collection of brown fat, mature fat, and atrial myocytes located within the limbus of the fossa ovalis {9577955}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 443,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67457,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 443,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 487,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 444,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67458,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 444,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Diagnostic molecular pathology is not usually required. <em>MDM2</em> amplification studies can be performed if there is concern for well-differentiated liposarcoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67459,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "<h5>Lipoma</h5>\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Encapsulated mass composed of mature adipocytes</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h5>LHAS</h5>\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Collection of immature (brown) fat, mature (yellow) fat, and atrial myocytes within the atrial septum</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>&ge;&nbsp;15 mm in thickness</li>\r\n</ul>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-02T09:31:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 445,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67460,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 445,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 489,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 446,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67461,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 446,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lipomas and LHAS typically do not require surgery unless the patient is symptomatic. Tumours requiring surgical intervention can usually be completely excised without complications {2617502; 6381889; 2322057; 29992619}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]